/-- Whenever the function returns a result r, for every balanced string t (as defined by the grammar B ::= ε | '(' B '))' B) such that s is a subsequence of t, len(t) >= n + r.
  Preconditions: s is a byte slice of length n with 1 <= n <= 100000, and for every i with 0 <= i < n, s[i] is either 40 or 41. -/
theorem spec_11 (s : Slice Std.U8) (n : ℕ)
    (hn : 1 ≤ n) (hn_ub : n ≤ 100000) (hlen : s.length = n) (hparen : IsParenSlice s) :
